/-!
# Toward the descent of the marked full-flag strata: declaration and axiom audit

**Status.** Two pieces of the one-adjoint-site ring statement are Lean theorems, for all
parameters.

* **The joint-ideal equation.** Over any commutative ring, for any polynomial `P` and any
  `r, j, h, s`, the top-row `j`-minor ideal of `(t^(h+1), s t^h)` modulo `P` is
  `G_j(t^(h+1)) + (s) G_j(t^h)` (`jointTopIdeal_eq_sup`). Hence, for every block `q`, every `h`
  and every `j`,
  `adjointSiteJointTopIdeal q h j = adjointSiteRemainderTopIdeal q h (h+1) j ⊔
    (s) * adjointSiteRemainderTopIdeal q h h j` (`adjointSiteJointTopIdeal_eq_sup`). This is the
  third conjunct of `OneAdjointStratumCount B k`, for every `B` and `k`.
* **Complement form of the one-minor ideals.** In a coinvariant alphabet, with `Y` nonempty,
  `Z = Yᶜ`, `r = |Y|`: the top row of `t^m mod P_Y` is the coefficient of `t^(m+1-r)` in
  `∏_Z (1 - x t)` (`topRemainder_eq_complement`); the one-minor ideal of `(t^L)` is generated by
  these coefficients from `L + 1 - r` on (`topIdeal_one_power_complement`); it is `(∏ Z)` at the
  top and `(∏ Z, c(Z))` one step lower. The joint one-minor ideal is `(∏ Z, s c(Z))` on the singly
  marked flag with one double (`jointTopIdeal_one_eq_pair`, `n = h + 2`) and `(∏ Z, c(Z))` on the
  doubly marked flag (`jointTopIdeal_one_eq_pair_of_zero`, `s = 0`, `n = h + 3`). These are
  exactly the ideals whose dimensions are bounded below in `SL4TMarkedFlagStrataJointAudit`.

**Not proved here.** `OneAdjointStratumCount B 1` remains open; its first two conjuncts
(`dim A ≤ w₀`, `dim A/G_j ≤ w₀ - w_j`) are open. Open nodes:

* the two-minor ideal of the doubly marked flag in complement form, `G_2 = ((∏ Z)²)` (Hankel
  minors of the complete functions of `Y`);
* the vanishing `G_j = 0` above the T-point count and the deformation lower bound
  `dim C/G_j ≥ #(configurations with fewer than j T-points)`, as an equivariant identification of
  `C/G_j` with the graded configuration ring;
* the presentation of `AdjointSiteCoefficientRing (mixedLabelBlockParams 1 B d e₁ e₂) (B - 1)` as
  the colour invariants of the marked full flag, the descent of `G_j`, and the orbit count
  `adjointSiteWordCount`.

Axioms of every declaration are printed below.
-/

